        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ab895b48-6341-57d1-b7c2-5a135f2e9b99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jamelão, José Bispo Clementino dos Santos\n- Organizations: Mangueira\n- Events: Rio Carnival, Carnaval, Lent\n- Roles: samba singer, tamborim player, official singer\n\nFacts:\n- José Bispo Clementino dos Santos was born on May 12, 1913, and became known as the Brazilian samba singer Jamelão.\n- Jamelão began his music career as a tamborim player.\n- From 1949 to 2006, Jamelão performed in every Carnaval as the official singer for the samba school Mangueira's parades.\n- The Carnival in Rio de Janeiro is a festival held every year before Lent.\n- The Rio Carnival is considered the biggest carnival in the world and draws 2 million people per day onto the streets.\n- Jamelão died on June 14, 2008.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1c6f29db-6d63-5759-9db9-bf53547c8921",
        "text": "Page: Jamelão. Sentence: José Bispo Clementino dos Santos (May 12, 1913 – June 14, 2008) was a Brazilian samba singer known as Jamelão (] ).\nPage: Jamelão. Sentence: He began in music as a tamborim player, but later became known as the official singer at samba school Mangueira's carnaval parades, performing in every Carnaval from 1949 to 2006.\nPage: Rio Carnival. Sentence: The Carnival in Rio de Janeiro (Portuguese: Carnaval) is a festival held every year before Lent and considered the biggest carnival in the world with 2 million people per day on the streets.",
